looped-transformer-toy demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/looped-transformer-toy/) is a CPU-only clear-experiment
toy inspired by:

  Ekbote, Pagnoni, Sachan, Bhosale, Lewis, Fazel-Zarandi, Rajput, Gonugondla,
  "How to Loop Your Transformer: Loop Scaling, Specialization, and Parallel
  Inference", FAIR at Meta / MIT, arXiv:2610.40325 (October 2026)
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.40325
  https://arxiv.org/html/2610.40325v1

Found via a bookmarked X post by @iScienceLuvr:
  https://x.com/iScienceLuvr/status/2116286474090107140

No official code repository was located as of 2026-10-31 (searched arXiv
abstract/HTML; Hugging Face Papers for 2610.40325 returned 404). This app is
therefore an **independent clean-room toy** of full-stack weight-shared
looping on synthetic multi-digit addition — NOT a reproduction of the paper's
up-to-1B-parameter language-model / DCLM tables.

No warranty. Research / demo use. Trained weights stay out of git (work/ is
git-ignored).
